res\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"405ae1367ad6eabc78f57804884de5e44d6c1926a32fff290ee3e1c019ff3143","event_uuid":"69bc5cd7-9b45-4bbc-84dc-8b8dca28c50a","position":{"commit_sha":"ca0049881e5017d907830d046ad70b795bfda0b6","position":"1786248183048231001-69bc5cd7-9b45-4bbc-84dc-8b8dca28c50a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e18d494a964f5bf7c79cde23550e6d11e7a6860371c8a523e265632e4d612849","event_uuid":"4167690c-4665-4586-a28e-74bab5defdb6","position":{"commit_sha":"d07f9343d2c89f489ac16fed1a951a5b93bc5d66","position":"1786248294348865001-4167690c-4665-4586-a28e-74bab5defdb6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7755d5d4c46d8955709eeda11b70c23f71000d4eff660452291b71c529545763","event_uuid":"a26ca82a-11a3-4fa0-9cbc-2445227b656e","position":{"commit_sha":"2d995e82feaaa3e25ba85e6a396fcc12cf475798","position":"1786248297870243001-a26ca82a-11a3-4fa0-9cbc-2445227b656e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"duplicate","comments":[],"created_at":1786142205076139001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"05fe0b7f-17af-4cfc-9fc4-211f25443646","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9f63-16dc-f014-4df2"},{"link_uuid":"eddc4612-94c8-407c-a1e7-9522e7c2ee12","relation":"duplicates","target_id":"3b93-a64e-693d-4f5e"}],"description":"## Discovered while landing bug 9f63\n\n`89d5-61da-b621-47f8` owns the py3.11 CI cell instability, but it is CLOSED, so this preventable defect would otherwise live only as a comment on a closed ticket. Filing it open, because it is a guard we do not have and it cost a landing cycle.\n\n## What happened\n\nA new test in `tests/unit/test_review_bot_in_flight.py` used the idiomatic-looking\n\n```python\nwith TestClient(app) as client:\n    ...\n```\n\nto assert ONE field of the `/health` JSON body. Entering `TestClient` as a context manager runs the app **lifespan**, which:\n\n* starts the queue worker,\n* starts the **real** `reconcile_loop` (`app.py`) — every other lifespan-entering test in that module stubs it with `_idle_reconcile_loop` (`tests/unit/test_review_bot.py:1462, :1490, :1631`),\n* starts the snapshot janitor, whose `startup_sweep` is a genuine filesystem walk (`src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py:282` -> `src/rebar/_snapshot/cache.py:133 entry_size`),\n* and on exit awaits `queue.join()` under `shutdown_drain_seconds()` — a **1200-second** window.\n\nUnder coverage tracing on the py3.11 cell that combination wedged an xdist worker. The suite reached 99% and produced no further output until the 60-minute job timeout, three runs in a row.\n\n## Why it was expensive to find\n\nIt presents exactly like the runner-side flake it is not. Three of four matrix cells passed; the review-bot test files passed in isolation; the full suite passed on 3.11 *without* `--cov`. Only the complete CI command reproduces it. Attribution needed a controlled A/B:\n\n| tree | py3.11 + coverage + xdist, CI's exact command |\n| --- | --- |\n| clean `origin/main` @ 1afdbbd0be | 11184 passed, 26 skipped, **16m11s** |\n| the branch | **hung at 99%** |\n\nand then `faulthandler` (`timeout -s ABRT`) to see a worker holding a live anyio blocking portal alongside the janitor thread mid-sweep.\n\n## Why a guard is worth it\n\nNothing in the repo makes any of this visible at the call site. `with TestClient(app)` reads like a normal client construction; the 20-minute drain, the live reconciler and the disk walk are all invisible consequences. The existing convention — stub `reconcile_loop` — is real but undocumented and unenforced, so it is followed by imitation and lost by anyone who writes a fresh test.\n\n## Fix sketch\n\nCheapest useful version, in rough order of value:\n\n1. A shared fixture (e.g. `review_bot_client`) that enters the lifespan with `reconcile_loop` stubbed, the janitor disabled and `shutdown_drain_seconds` overridden to something test-scaled, so the safe path is also the easy path.\n2. A test-lint or `conftest` assertion that fails fast when the review-bot app lifespan is entered without the reconciler stub, naming the fixture to use.\n3. Prefer awaiting the handler directly when a test only asserts a response payload — the route returns the dict as-is, so the contract is identical and nothing background starts. (That is what bug 9f63's change ended up doing.)\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] A test that enters the review-bot app lifespan without stubbing `reconcile_loop` fails fast with a message naming the correct fixture, rather than hanging\n- [x] The shared fixture bounds `shutdown_drain_seconds` to a test-scaled value, proven by a test asserting the teardown completes in seconds\n- [x] The snapshot janitor does not perform a real filesystem sweep under that fixture\n- [x] The convention is stated where a test author will see it, not only inherited by imitation\n\n## 2026-08-08 resolution evidence\n\nThe ordinary review-bot app lifespan now completes promptly without per-test dependency stubs; the exact regression test passed. Canonical implementation: 3b93-a64e-693d-4f5e.\n","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"4167690c-4665-4586-a28e-74bab5defdb6","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4a11-aecf-4d33-45ae","ticket_type":"bug","title":"A test entering the review-bot app lifespan silently inherits a 1200s shutdown drain, a real reconciler and a filesystem sweep — nothing stops the next one","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5c1e6335-31eb-4dab-99ed-ae106f3da81d","05fe0b7f-17af-4cfc-9fc4-211f25443646","eddc4612-94c8-407c-a1e7-9522e7c2ee12","df2f6bc6-8ea2-4472-bfbe-b41cdea0b332","851b3f54-5cb2-47f9-b534-d10c76418a24","69bc5cd7-9b45-4bbc-84dc-8b8dca28c50a","4167690c-4665-4586-a28e-74bab5defdb6","a26ca82a-11a3-4fa0-9cbc-2445227b656e"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659582885207001,"uuid":"e35725bf-fa18-4fa6-8484-b932bef0c1bd"}